#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Lives from afar" tvg-id="2006807810" tvg-name="The Sulawesi Pinisi is a highly manoeuvrable cargo sailing vessel. During the Dutch colonial era‚ it was used to sail between the Indonesian islands‚ carrying everything from simple goods to precious commodities for export‚ particularly spices. The art of making these handsome ships was inscribed on the UNESCO list of Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity in 2017.<br/>From 21.11.2023 10:53" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",360° Reportage - Sulawesi: The Art of Boat Building (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (21.11.2023)
https://arteptweb-a.akamaihd.net/am/ptweb/111000/111600/111684-012-A_SQ_0_VOEU-STE%5BANG%5D_08379212_MP4-2200_AMM-PTWEB-101134702613003_2CXxA1Ds2jk.mp4
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Lives from afar" tvg-id="1335045991" tvg-name="Infamous drug baron Pablo Escobar had four hippos flown over from Africa to populate his very own zoo on his private estate in Columbia. After his death in 1993‚ the hippos escaped and have been colonising local waterways ever since. Conservationists are now waging a war against this invasive species which is harmful to the local ecosystem and highly dangerous to humans.<br/>From 03.11.2023 14:29" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Pablo Escobar's Hippos - Geo Reportage (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (03.11.2023)
https://arteptweb-a.akamaihd.net/am/ptweb/101000/101100/101139-008-A_SQ_0_VOEU-STE%5BANG%5D_08316514_MP4-2200_AMM-PTWEB-101073885523748_2BhFS1Cehqb.mp4
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Lives from afar" tvg-id="206512212" tvg-name="In the village of Asau in north-east Romania‚ locals take part in the annual bear dance. The pre-Christian rite is a joyful occasion where bear-skin wearing dancers take to the streets in a lively procession that expresses local identity.<br/>From 19.01.2024 18:03" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Romanian Bear Dancers (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (19.01.2024)
