#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Planet Earth" tvg-id="568561506" tvg-name="The Humboldt current flows from the cold Antarctic up the South American coast to the equator. On the barren coast of Peru lies the Punta San Juan nature reserve where the largest population of guano cormorants in the world lives. Further north at the equator‚ swarms of giant manta rays glide through the sea and a female blue whale drifts leisurely west to reach the Galapagos Islands. Over million.....<br/>From 14.11.2023 05:00" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",The Humboldt Current - From Peru to the Galapagos Islands (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (14.11.2023)
