#EXTINF:-1 group-title="History - Civilisations" tvg-id="1327560668" tvg-name="The ceremonial smoking pipe is Amerindian‚ but without a name from the Amerindian language. It was 'discovered' by French and British colonists who came into contact with the indigenous population in the 17th century. Amerindians then boarded French ships and took the pipe to the other side of the Atlantic‚ where it quickly became popular.<br/>From 04.12.2021 05:00" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Making History - Ceremonial Smoking Pipes: Conflict and Resolution (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (04.12.2021)
