#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sciences - In brief" tvg-id="269598664" tvg-name="Wind speeds on the planet are decreasing. Gusts are driven by the temperature difference between the equator and the Earth's poles. As the climate warms‚ the temperature gap narrows‚ and the winds falter. In recent times‚ researchers have observed a weakening of a particularly important wind - the jet stream. As the jet stream drives high and low-pressure systems over our continents‚ its slowdown .....<br/>From 23.07.2023 17:48" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",42: The Answer to Almost Everything - Earth's Changing Winds (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (23.07.2023)
